@cclerget can you please take a look?  I too always only see the devpts mount including gid=5.

I see [code](https://github.com/apptainer/apptainer/blob/main/internal/pkg/runtime/engine/apptainer/container_linux.go#L1352) that is avoiding setting gid=5, and debug messages show the code is running when I add the `-c` option, but still the mount point includes gid=5.  I also did a test build removing the gid=5 from the one other place in the [code](https://github.com/apptainer/apptainer/blob/main/internal/pkg/runtime/engine/config/oci/config.go#L186) but that also didn't make a difference.  I am guessing that without `-c` it gets bindmounted in directly from the host and that preserves the option, but don't have an explanation with `-c`.

By the way, the grantpt problem fix referred to in the original issue was [backported to el7](https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1522992).

Thank you for the report.  I can reproduce this also with apptainer-1.0.0.  With the debug option I can see that it happens when reading `/.singularity.d/env/90-environment.sh` which is the script that gets everything from the `%environment` section.  If I replace `cd /usr` with `pwd` the problem does not happen.

