@bloer Note that osg34 has not been supported for quite some time (and osg35 does not distribute singularity) so the singularity on your system should be upgraded from the current version in epel, which is version 3.8.6.  Version 3.6.4 was a security release, so 3.6.3 should not be run anymore.

@soichih @DrDaveD Not sure about the right fix there, either we could set the BlobInfoCacheDir to point to a path based on hostname so cache would be isolated based on host, but it might not cover the case of multiple apptainer instances on the same host, I know that boltdb can handle multi-thread (with internal lock) but not sure about multiple processes.
Second option would be to force the in-memory cache of `github.com/containers/image` package with a dirty hack but might impact performance during image conversion.

Between @soichih have you tried with the latest version singularity (or apptainer v1.0.0) ? Because `github.com/containers/image/v3` is old and apptainer/singularity latest releases are using `github.com/containers/image/v5`, maybe there might be some changes.

